GTKThemeTest 0.4 - riscos-gtk theme test

Every common GTK 3 widget in the RISCOS theme, in one window, through
riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend. Everything you do is shown in the status
line at the bottom and written to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.GTKThemeTest.Log.

Pages
  Buttons and fields   action, shaded, toggle and linked buttons; a link;
                       writable, empty, password and shaded fields; a
                       display field; a number range (adjuster arrows);
                       a pop-up; a writable with a menu; styled text.
  Options and sliders  option and radio icons (on, off, mixed, shaded);
                       a switch; sliders, progress and level bars.
  Lists and text       a long list and a tree with scroll bars; a text
                       view with both scroll bars.
  Dialogues and menus  a message dialogue; a popover; a context menu
                       (click Menu in the box); info bars; a calendar.
The menu bar at the top (File, Edit, View with ticks and a Zoom submenu,
Help) and the Cancel / Apply buttons (Apply is the default action
button) are on every page. Hover for interactive help (tooltips).

Please try everything, then send back the Log, a photo or screenshot of
each page and of an open menu, and a note of anything that looks or
behaves differently from RISC OS.

New in 0.4: the tab area no longer jumps when Apply (the default
button) is clicked and takes the focus.

New in 0.3: menu text no longer garbled when a menu bar menu first
opens; after releasing the mouse over a menu (or anywhere outside the
window) the next click goes where it should (before, it reopened the
menu bar menu). For a menu trace in the Log: *Set RISCOS_GTK_MENU_DEBUG 1
before running; *Set RISCOS_GTK_DEBUG 1 also logs mouse buttons.

New in 0.2: menus are real Wimp menus. The menu bar's menus open below
their titles, pop-ups open to the right of the field, the context menu
opens at the pointer; keyboard short-cuts are shown in a column, ticks
and shaded entries as usual, submenus (View > Zoom) open from the
arrow. A click elsewhere or Escape closes a menu; choosing with Adjust
keeps it open (try View > Show grid with Adjust).

Known, not done yet:
- No clipboard between programs yet, no drag and drop, pointer shapes
  are the normal arrow.
- Menus have no keyboard navigation of the menu bar itself (F10).

Needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16+ and ARMEABISupport (PackMan), and a 32bpp
(16 million colour) desktop with RISC OS 5.21 or later.

